      <div type="clause" n="84.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 84.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="84.2" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="368" ed="#liebermann"/>And gesælig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_84-2.lnote.oe.13"/> byð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IICn_84-2.lnote.oe.14"/> se hyrde, þe þonne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IICn_84-2.lnote.oe.15"/> ða heorde into Godes rice ⁊ to heofonlicre myrhþe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IICn_84-2.lnote.oe.16"/> bliðe mot lædan for<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IICn_84-2.lnote.oe.17"/> ærran gewyrhtan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="84.2" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="368" ed="#liebermann"/>And geselig byð se hyrde, ðe ðonne ða heorde into Godes rice ⁊ to heofenlicre myrðe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_84-2.lnote.oe.3"/> bliðe mot lædan for his<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#IICn_84-2.lnote.oe.star2"/> ærran gewyrhtan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="84.2" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="368" ed="#liebermann"/>And gesalig bið se hyrde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_84-2.lnote.oe.6"/>, þe þonne þa heorde into Godes rice ⁊ to heofonolicre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_84-2.lnote.oe.3-2"/> myrðe bliðe mot lædan for ærran gewyrhtan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="84.2" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="369" ed="#liebermann"/>Et felix erit pastor, qui tunc gregem suum in Dei divitias et celeste gaudium letum perducere<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_84-2.lnote.oe.7"/> poterit ex pristinis operibus.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="84.2" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="369" ed="#liebermann"/>Felix ille pastor, qui tunc gregem suum in regnum et celestes delicias letus introducere meruit propter precedentia merita!</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="84.2" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="216" ed="#robertson"/>And geselig byð se hyrde ðe ðonne ða heorde into Godes rice ⁊ to heofenlicre myrðe bliðe mot lædan for ærran<ptr type="editorNote" n="12" target="#IICn_84-2.robnote.fn.12"/> gewyrhtan.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="296" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And gesælig byð se hyrde þe þonne ða heorde into Godes rice and to heofonlicre myrhþe bliðe mot lædan for ærran gewyrhtan.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="369" ed="#liebermann"/>Und selig wird der Hirt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_84-2.lnote.de.1"/> sein, der dann die Herde in Gottes Reich<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_84-2.lnote.de.2"/> und zur himmlischen Wonne freudig einführen darf wegen [ihrer] früheren Thaten.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And blessed will be the shepherd who may then joyfully lead the flock into God's kingdom and to heavenly bliss because of [their] earlier deeds.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_84-2.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="217" ed="#robertson"/>And blessed is the shepherd who then may gladly lead his flock into the kingdom of God and to the joy of Heaven, because of the works which they have wrought.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="297" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And blessed is the shepherd who may then happily lead his flock into the kingdom of God and into heavenly bliss for the deeds they have done.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">BR: added from Gesetze I p. 369, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">for ærran: for his ærran B</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84-2.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">369</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ergänze</hi> Dei</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supply Dei</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84-2.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">368</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84-2.lnote.oe.star2" n="**" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">368</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">falsch</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">wrong</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84-2.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">369</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">prod. <hi rend="italic">KHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">prod. KHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84-2.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">368</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">über</hi> æ <hi rend="italic">neu</hi> a <hi rend="italic">G</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">a written above æ by a later hand G</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84-2.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">368</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">biþ ða h. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">biþ ða h. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84-2.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">368</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">darüber neu</hi> þonre <hi rend="italic">G</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þonre written above by a later hand G</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84-2.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">368</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">myrþe <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">myrþe Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84-2.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">368</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">his <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">his added by Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84-2.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">368</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">r <hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">r written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84-2.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">368</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_84-2.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">214</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Hirt und Herde I 26, 1—3</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Shepherd and flock I 26, 1—3</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_84-2.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">214</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Q wählt unter den Bedd. von <hi rend="italic">rice</hi> falsch.—Von Himmelswonne spricht Cn 1020, 20 und sechsmal in I. II Cn</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Q chooses wrongly among the meanings of <hi rend="italic">rice</hi>.—Heavenly bliss is spoken of in Cn 1020, 20 and six times in I. II Cn</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_84-2.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. I Cn. 26, 1–3.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_84-2.robnote.fn.12" n="12" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">216</biblScope></bibl><label>ærran</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">G, A; <hi rend="italic">his ærran</hi> B.</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
